content_list.content:
Excellent. Since the **Protocol** is the contract between the Agent and the Server, we must define it first. Then, we will build the **C Linux Agent** to collect the data, and finally the **Go Backend** to ingest it. 

This completes **Tasks 6, 7, and 8** from your roadmap.

---

### Step 1: Define the Protocol (Task 6)

Create the JSON schemas that dictate exactly how the Agent and Server communicate. This ensures strict validation on both sides.

**File: `protocol/telemetry.schema.json`**
```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "title": "SentriX Telemetry Payload",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["agent_id", "timestamp", "sequence", "metrics"],
  "properties": {
    "agent_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
    "timestamp": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
    "sequence": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
    "metrics": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["name", "value", "unit"],
        "properties": {
          "name": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^system\\.[a-z0-9_]+\\.[a-z0-9_]+$" },
          "value": { "type": "number" },
          "unit": { "type": "string", "enum": ["percent", "bytes", "bytes_per_sec", "count", "seconds"] },
          "labels": { "type": "object", "additionalProperties": { "type": "string" } }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**File: `protocol/enrollment.schema.json`**
```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "title": "SentriX Agent Enrollment",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["token", "hostname", "platform", "architecture", "agent_version"],
  "properties": {
    "token": { "type": "string" },
    "hostname": { "type": "string" },
    "platform": { "type": "string", "enum": ["linux", "windows"] },
    "architecture": { "type": "string", "enum": ["x86_64", "arm64"] },
